cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Histopathology Molecular Subtype Classification"
message: "If you refer to this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Zanoni
    given-names: Alessandro
  - family-names: Valentini
    given-names: Jacopo
  - family-names: Balducci
    given-names: Arianna
  - family-names: Gallicola
    given-names: Renato
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2025-12-16"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Solution to the second challenge of the Artificial Neural Networks and Deep
  Learning course (Politecnico di Milano, A.Y. 2025/26): classifying the
  molecular subtype of human tissue from low-magnification whole-slide images.
  Slides are cut into 256x256 tiles under a multiple-instance-learning framing
  and classified by a weighted ensemble of a ResNet18 tile classifier, evaluated
  under the full dihedral group at inference, and a linear head over frozen UNI
  embeddings. The ensemble weight is selected by grid search on out-of-fold
  slide probabilities.
keywords:
  - computational pathology
  - whole-slide imaging
  - multiple instance learning
  - foundation models
  - ensemble methods
  - PyTorch
